summary:
Abe proves the Langlands correspondence for overconvergent F-isocrystals on curves over finite fields (Theorem 4.2.2): irreducible Q̄_p-isocrystals of rank r with finite determinant on open subsets of a curve X correspond to cuspidal automorphic representations of GL_r(A_F) with finite central character, with matching Frobenius and Hecke eigenvalues and local L- and ε-factors of pairs. Hence every lisse ℓ-adic sheaf with finite determinant on a curve has a crystalline companion (Theorem 4.4.1, Deligne's 'petits camarades'). The proof follows L. Lafforgue with p-adic cohomology: the p-adic principe de récurrence (Abe, with the Abe–Marmora product formula) reduces to constructing A_r → I_r, which is done by the cohomology of Lafforgue's (compactified) moduli of shtukas, his negligibility arguments, the Hecke action on the essential part and a trace computation transported from the ℓ-adic side by ℓ-independence of traces of correspondences. To make this possible the paper builds a six-operation formalism for holonomic arithmetic D-modules beyond realizable schemes: on realizable schemes, Beilinson's equivalence, Ind-categories, the constructible t-structure, extension of scalars to Q̄_p and trace maps for flat morphisms (§1); derived categories on algebraic stacks (and so on all separated algebraic spaces of finite type) by simplicial presentations, and the six operations with duality, Poincaré duality and weights on admissible and c-admissible stacks (§2); cycle classes, correspondences and ℓ-independence of their traces after Kato–Saito (§3); and Lefschetz, Čebotarev and Gabber–Fujiwara in the appendix.
Routes:
- §§1–3 and the appendix join the pending Part II PadicDifferentialEquationsPartIIArithmeticDModules (proposed by PAPER-XU-ZHU-22, whose brief already names this paper as its main source);
- §4 and the introduction form a new Part II of GlobalShtukasAndFunctionFieldLanglands for the Langlands correspondence with p-adic coefficients and crystalline companions, since GS.6 plans Lafforgue's ℓ-adic theorem only and the pending companion Part IIs source-gate or exclude the crystalline side;
- Lafforgue's moduli of shtukas are planned at GS.2/GS.6.
Source issues, each checked by hand:
- in the foundations: the modified dual on stacks has the wrong twist sign; the proof of the weight bound for push-forwards (2.2.32(6), hence Theorem 2.3.38(i), used in §4) does not follow from the cited spectral sequence; the argument for independence of the Frobenius lift in Remark 1.1.2 is false; Lemma 2.2.4(iii) and Remark 2.3.1 need 'surjective';
- in §3: the multiplicativity of the degrees d_Γ and the ring-homomorphism property of 'norm' fail for stacks with generic stabilisers, the remark on generic fibres of correspondences is false, and the normal-cone claim behind Lemma 3.2.6 holds only for immersions;
- in the appendix: the Lefschetz formula A.3.2 has the wrong exponent, the stacky trace formula A.5.1 is false for n ≥ 2 as stated, and the definition of compatible systems is vacuous at points of degree > 1 as written;
- misprints, including a sign in the pole corollary of 4.3.3 and the page numbers of Weil II.
None of them is known to invalidate the main theorems, which later work (Kedlaya, Abe–Esnault) has used and extended.
